module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Submodule
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.ModuleComparison

/-!
# The pullback of a presheaf of modules is generated by the image of the unit

Mathlib defines `PresheafOfModules.pullback φ` as the left adjoint of
`PresheafOfModules.pushforward φ`, assembled from free presheaves on representables, and gives **no
description of its sections**: there is no base-change formula `f^* P = 𝒪 ⊗_{f^{-1}𝒪'} f^{-1} P`,
and no lemma computing the unit on sections.  This file proves the half of the base-change
description that the adjunction alone determines, namely the *generation* half.

For `ψ : P ⟶ (pushforward φ).obj Q` with transpose `ψ^♯ : (pullback φ).obj P ⟶ Q`, the image of
`ψ^♯` over an object is exactly the submodule generated by the restrictions of the image of `ψ`
(`PresheafOfModules.range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule`).  Taking `ψ` to be the unit and
`ψ^♯ = 𝟙`, this says that **`(pullback φ).obj P` is generated, over every object, by the
restrictions of the image of the unit `P ⟶ (pushforward φ).obj ((pullback φ).obj P)`**
(`PresheafOfModules.generatedSubmodule_unit_eq_top`): the statement that, for a base change of
modules `N ↦ B ⊗_A N`, says that `B ⊗_A N` is generated over `B` by the elements `1 ⊗ n`.

The intended application is the step `R^p g_* = 0` of [Stacks, Tag 07JN].  Hypothesis (2) of that
proposition is the surjectivity of the comparison map `c_f : f^* F_{T'} ⟶ F_T`
(`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.CohomologyRestriction.IsSurjectiveComparison`),
and the source's proof passes from it to the surjectivity of the `f`-map `F_{T'} ⟶ f_* F_T` with
the words "surjectivity of `c_f` is equivalent to surjectivity of `F_{T'} ⟶ f_* F_T`".  That
passage is exactly the generation statement above, and it is what this file supplies.

## Main definitions

* `PresheafOfModules.generatedSubmodule φ ψ` — for `ψ : P ⟶ (pushforward φ).obj Q`, the
  sub-presheaf of modules of `Q` generated by the image of `ψ`: over an object `Y` it is the
  `R.obj Y`-submodule spanned by the restrictions along all `F(X) ⟶ Y` of the sections
  `ψ.app X s`.
* `PresheafOfModules.toGeneratedSubmodule φ ψ` — the corestriction of `ψ` to that sub-presheaf.

## Main results

* `PresheafOfModules.range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule` — **the image of the transpose
  `ψ^♯` is, over every object, the submodule generated by the image of `ψ`.**
* `PresheafOfModules.generatedSubmodule_unit_eq_top` — **the pullback is generated by the image of
  the unit**, the special case `ψ = unit`.
* `range_moduleComparison_app_eq_fmapSubmodule`, in the namespace
  `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.CohomologyRestriction` — the crystalline
  reading: over every open of the ambient scheme the image of `c_f : f^* F_{T'} ⟶ F_T` is the
  `𝒪_T`-submodule generated by the image of the `f`-map.
* `isLocallySurjective_fmapSubmodule_ι`, in the same namespace — under hypothesis (2) of
  [Stacks, Tag 07JN], `F_T` is locally generated by the image of the `f`-map, for every morphism
  of `Cris(X/S)` whose map on ambient schemes is a closed immersion.

## What is and is not proved

The general results carry **no hypotheses at all** beyond the existence of the pullback: no
affineness, no quasi-coherence, no flatness, no local freeness.  In particular the affine case is
not a special case that had to be isolated — the *pullback description* proved here is general, and
affineness enters only in the *surjectivity consequence* discussed below.

What is proved is the generation half of the base-change description, and only that half.  The
adjunction determines the image of the transpose and nothing else, so this file says which
submodule of `Q` the map `ψ^♯` surjects onto; it does not produce an isomorphism
`f^* P ≅ 𝒪 ⊗_{f^{-1}𝒪'} f^{-1} P`.  The missing half is injectivity, which is false in general and
needs flatness or a presentation; a consumer that needs to *invert* a canonical map out of a
pullback (for instance to give a connection the target `F_T ⊗_{𝒪_T} Ω_{T/S,δ}` rather than the
ideal of the diagonal, as in [Stacks, Tag 07J6]) is not unblocked by what is here, while a consumer
that needs surjectivity or generation is.

The consequence that [Stacks, Tag 07JN] actually consumes — surjectivity of the *transition maps*
`F(U', T', δ') ⟶ F(U, T, δ)`, the interface
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.HasSurjectiveLevelRestrictions` — is **not**
proved here, and the gap is not the pullback.  Two further steps separate it from
`isLocallySurjective_fmapSubmodule_ι`.  First, the submodule generated by the image of the `f`-map
collapses to that image only when the ring map `𝒪_{T'}(W') ⟶ 𝒪_T(f^{-1}W')` is surjective, which
for a closed immersion holds over affine `W'`; on the big crystalline category that is
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.surjective_appTop_restrictOpenMap`.  This is the one place
where affineness is needed, and it is needed for the surjectivity consequence, not for the
pullback description, which is proved above in full generality.

Second, and this is the real wall, local surjectivity on `T'` gives
surjectivity on global sections over an affine `T'` only through the source's cohomological
argument: the kernel `K` of `F_{T'} ⟶ f_* F_T` is quasi-coherent, and `H^1(T', K) = 0` because `T'`
is affine.  That argument needs the quasi-coherence of the kernel, which this file does not have:
hypothesis (1) of the proposition is *local* quasi-coherence of `F`, so the identification of `K`
as a quasi-coherent module is a separate step.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry Opposite TopologicalSpace
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe v v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂ u

noncomputable section

namespace PresheafOfModules

section Generated

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D]
  {F : C ⥤ D} {R : Dᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}} {S : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}} (φ : S ⟶ F.op ⋙ R)
  {P : PresheafOfModules.{v} S} {Q : PresheafOfModules.{v} R}
  (ψ : P ⟶ (pushforward.{v} φ).obj Q)

/-- The restriction map of a presheaf of modules along an identity morphism is the identity. -/
private theorem map_id_apply (N : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) {Y : Dᵒᵖ} (x : N.obj Y) :
    N.map (𝟙 Y) x = x := by
  rw [N.map_id]
  simp only [ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'_inv_app, ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'App_inv_apply]
  rfl


/-- The restriction map of a presheaf of modules along an identity morphism is the identity, as a
statement about the bundled semilinear restriction maps. -/
private theorem restrictₛₗ_id_apply (N : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) {Y : Dᵒᵖ} (x : N.obj Y) :
    N.restrictₛₗ (𝟙 Y) x = x := by
  rw [restrictₛₗ_apply, N.map_id]
  simp only [ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'_inv_app, ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'App_inv_apply]

/-- The bundled semilinear restriction maps of a presheaf of modules compose. -/
private theorem restrictₛₗ_comp_apply (N : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) {X Y Z : Dᵒᵖ}
    (f : X ⟶ Y) (g : Y ⟶ Z)
    (x : N.obj X) : N.restrictₛₗ g (N.restrictₛₗ f x) = N.restrictₛₗ (f ≫ g) x :=
  (N.map_comp_apply f g x).symm

/-- **The component of `ψ` over `X`, as a semilinear map into the sections of `Q` over `F(X)`.**
The sections of `(pushforward φ).obj Q` over `X` *are* the sections of `Q` over `F(X)`, with the
scalars restricted along `φ.app X`; this records the component of `ψ` with the latter as its
codomain, so that it can be composed with the restriction maps of `Q`. -/
def appₛₗ (X : Cᵒᵖ) : P.obj X →ₛₗ[(φ.app X).hom] Q.obj (op (F.obj X.unop)) :=
  (ModuleCat.semilinearMapAddEquiv (φ.app X).hom (P.obj X)
    (Q.obj (op (F.obj X.unop)))).symm (ψ.app X)

/-- The semilinear component `appₛₗ φ ψ X` takes the same values as `ψ.app X`. -/
theorem appₛₗ_apply (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : P.obj X) : appₛₗ φ ψ X s = ψ.app X s := rfl

/-- The sections of `Q` over an object `Y` that generate the image of `ψ`: the restrictions along
all morphisms `F(X) ⟶ Y` of the sections in the image of `ψ`.  This is the generating set of
`PresheafOfModules.generatedSubmodule`. -/
def pushforwardGenerators (Y : Dᵒᵖ) : Set (Q.obj Y) :=
  {y | ∃ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (h : op (F.obj X.unop) ⟶ Y) (s : P.obj X), y = Q.restrictₛₗ h (appₛₗ φ ψ X s)}

/-- A section of `Q` over `Y` is a generator if and only if it is the restriction along some
`F(X) ⟶ Y` of a section in the image of `ψ` over `X`. -/
theorem mem_pushforwardGenerators {Y : Dᵒᵖ} {y : Q.obj Y} :
    y ∈ pushforwardGenerators φ ψ Y ↔
      ∃ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (h : op (F.obj X.unop) ⟶ Y) (s : P.obj X), y = Q.restrictₛₗ h (appₛₗ φ ψ X s) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- **The sub-presheaf of modules of `Q` generated by the image of `ψ`.**  Over an object `Y` it is
the `R.obj Y`-submodule spanned by the restrictions of the sections in the image of `ψ`; the family
is stable under restriction because a restriction of such a restriction is again one. -/
def generatedSubmodule : Q.Submodule where
  obj Y := Submodule.span (R.obj Y) (pushforwardGenerators φ ψ Y)
  map {Y Y'} t := by
    refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
    rintro y ⟨X, h, s, rfl⟩
    refine Submodule.mem_comap.2 ?_
    rw [restrictₛₗ_comp_apply]
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨X, h ≫ t, s, rfl⟩

/-- Over an object `Y`, the generated sub-presheaf is the `R.obj Y`-span of the generators. -/
theorem generatedSubmodule_obj (Y : Dᵒᵖ) :
    (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).obj Y = Submodule.span (R.obj Y) (pushforwardGenerators φ ψ Y) :=
  rfl

/-- The sections in the image of `ψ` lie in the sub-presheaf of modules they generate. -/
theorem appₛₗ_mem_generatedSubmodule (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : P.obj X) :
    appₛₗ φ ψ X s ∈ (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).obj (op (F.obj X.unop)) :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨X, 𝟙 _, s, (restrictₛₗ_id_apply Q _).symm⟩

/-- **The sub-presheaf of modules generated by the image of `ψ` is the smallest one whose sections
contain the image of `ψ`.**  Every generator is a restriction of a section in the image of `ψ`, and
a family of submodules stable under restriction contains those restrictions. -/
theorem generatedSubmodule_le {N : Q.Submodule}
    (hN : ∀ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : P.obj X), appₛₗ φ ψ X s ∈ N.obj (op (F.obj X.unop))) :
    generatedSubmodule φ ψ ≤ N := fun Y ↦ by
  refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
  rintro y ⟨X, h, s, rfl⟩
  exact N.map_mem h (hN X s)

/-- **The image of a morphism of presheaves of modules, as a sub-presheaf of modules of its
target.**  Over an object it is the range of the morphism there; the family is stable under
restriction by the naturality of the morphism. -/
def rangeSubmodule {Q' : PresheafOfModules.{v} R} (c : Q' ⟶ Q) : Q.Submodule where
  obj Y := LinearMap.range (c.app Y).hom
  map {Y Y'} t := by
    rintro y ⟨x, rfl⟩
    exact Submodule.mem_comap.2 ⟨Q'.restrictₛₗ t x, naturality_apply c t x⟩

/-- Over an object `Y`, the image sub-presheaf of `c` is the range of `c.app Y`. -/
theorem rangeSubmodule_obj {Q' : PresheafOfModules.{v} R} (c : Q' ⟶ Q) (Y : Dᵒᵖ) :
    (rangeSubmodule c).obj Y = LinearMap.range (c.app Y).hom :=
  rfl

/-- **The corestriction of `ψ` to the sub-presheaf of modules its image generates.**  Over an
object it is `ψ` with its values recorded as sections of the generated sub-presheaf. -/
def toGeneratedSubmodule :
    P ⟶ (pushforward.{v} φ).obj (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).toPresheafOfModules where
  app X := ModuleCat.semilinearMapAddEquiv (φ.app X).hom (P.obj X)
    ((generatedSubmodule φ ψ).toPresheafOfModules.obj (op (F.obj X.unop)))
    (LinearMap.codRestrict ((generatedSubmodule φ ψ).obj (op (F.obj X.unop))) (appₛₗ φ ψ X)
      (appₛₗ_mem_generatedSubmodule φ ψ X))
  naturality {X Y} t := by
    ext s
    exact Subtype.ext (naturality_apply ψ t s)

/-- The corestriction of `ψ` to the sub-presheaf of modules its image generates recovers `ψ` when
composed with the inclusion of that sub-presheaf. -/
theorem toGeneratedSubmodule_comp_ι :
    toGeneratedSubmodule φ ψ ≫ (pushforward.{v} φ).map (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).ι = ψ := by
  ext X s
  rfl

variable [(pushforward.{v} φ).IsRightAdjoint]

/-- **The transpose of `ψ` factors through the sub-presheaf of modules generated by the image of
`ψ`**, by the naturality of the adjunction bijection in the target. -/
theorem homEquivSymm_toGeneratedSubmodule_comp_ι :
    ((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P
        (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).toPresheafOfModules).symm (toGeneratedSubmodule φ ψ) ≫
      (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).ι =
    ((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ := by
  have h := Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_right_symm
    (pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ) (toGeneratedSubmodule φ ψ) (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).ι
  rw [toGeneratedSubmodule_comp_ι] at h
  exact h.symm

/-- **The image of the transpose of `ψ` is contained in the sub-presheaf of modules generated by
the image of `ψ`.**  This is the direction that needs the universal property of the pullback: the
transpose factors through the generated sub-presheaf, so its values are sections of that
sub-presheaf. -/
theorem range_homEquivSymm_app_le_generatedSubmodule (Y : Dᵒᵖ) :
    LinearMap.range ((((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ).app Y).hom ≤
      (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).obj Y := by
  rintro y ⟨x, rfl⟩
  have h := congrArg (fun α ↦ (α.app Y) x) (homEquivSymm_toGeneratedSubmodule_comp_ι φ ψ)
  simp only [comp_app] at h
  rw [← h]
  exact (((((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P
    (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).toPresheafOfModules).symm (toGeneratedSubmodule φ ψ)).app Y) x).2

/-- **The sections in the image of `ψ` are values of the transpose of `ψ`**, the transpose being
recovered from `ψ` by the unit of the adjunction. -/
theorem appₛₗ_mem_range_homEquivSymm_app (X : Cᵒᵖ) (s : P.obj X) :
    appₛₗ φ ψ X s ∈ LinearMap.range
      ((((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ).app
        (op (F.obj X.unop))).hom := by
  have hψ : ψ = (pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q
      (((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ) :=
    (Equiv.apply_symm_apply _ _).symm
  rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_unit] at hψ
  exact ⟨_, (congrArg (fun α ↦ (α.app X) s) hψ).symm⟩

/-- **The image of the transpose `ψ^♯ : (pullback φ).obj P ⟶ Q` of a morphism
`ψ : P ⟶ (pushforward φ).obj Q` is, over every object, exactly the submodule generated by the
restrictions of the image of `ψ`.**

This is the generation half of the base-change description of the pullback of presheaves of
modules, and it holds with no hypotheses: Mathlib's `PresheafOfModules.pullback` is only the left
adjoint of the pushforward, with no description of its sections, and the image of a transpose is
precisely what the adjunction does determine. -/
theorem range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule (Y : Dᵒᵖ) :
    LinearMap.range ((((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ).app Y).hom =
      (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).obj Y :=
  le_antisymm (range_homEquivSymm_app_le_generatedSubmodule φ ψ Y)
    (generatedSubmodule_le φ ψ
      (N := rangeSubmodule (((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ))
      (appₛₗ_mem_range_homEquivSymm_app φ ψ) Y)

/-- **The pullback of a presheaf of modules is generated by the image of the unit**: the
sub-presheaf of modules of `(pullback φ).obj P` generated by the image of the unit
`P ⟶ (pushforward φ).obj ((pullback φ).obj P)` is everything.

For a base change of modules `N ↦ B ⊗_A N` this is the statement that `B ⊗_A N` is generated over
`B` by the elements `1 ⊗ n`.  It is the special case of
`PresheafOfModules.range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule` in which `ψ` is the unit, whose
transpose is the identity. -/
theorem generatedSubmodule_unit_eq_top :
    generatedSubmodule (P := P) (Q := (pullback.{v} φ).obj P) φ
      ((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).unit.app P) = ⊤ := by
  have hid : ((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P
      ((pullback.{v} φ).obj P)).symm
        ((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).unit.app P) = 𝟙 _ :=
    ((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P _).symm_apply_eq.2
      (Adjunction.homEquiv_id _ _).symm
  refine PresheafOfModules.Submodule.ext fun Y ↦ ?_
  rw [← range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule, hid]
  simp

end Generated

end PresheafOfModules

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.CohomologyRestriction

variable {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} (M : PresheafOfModules.{u} (crisRing S))
  {A B : CrystallineThickening S} (g : A ⟶ B)

/-- **The sub-presheaf of `F_T` generated by the image of the `f`-map** of a morphism
`f : (U, T, δ) ⟶ (U', T', δ')` of `Cris(X/S)`: over an open `W` of `T` it is the
`𝒪_T(W)`-submodule spanned by the restrictions to `W` of the sections `F_{T'}(W') ⟶ F_T(f^{-1}W')`
of the `f`-map, for the opens `W'` of `T'` with `W ⊆ f^{-1}W'`. -/
abbrev fmapSubmodule : (moduleRestriction M A).Submodule :=
  PresheafOfModules.generatedSubmodule (restrictionFMap (crisRing S) g) (moduleFMap M g)

/-- **Over every open of the ambient scheme, the image of the comparison morphism
`c_f : f^* F_{T'} ⟶ F_T` is the `𝒪_T`-submodule generated by the image of the `f`-map
`F_{T'} ⟶ f_* F_T`.**

This is the step in the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JN] asserting that the surjectivity of `c_f` is
equivalent to the surjectivity of `F_{T'} ⟶ f_* F_T`: the comparison morphism is the transpose
of the `f`-map, and the image of a transpose is the submodule generated by the image of the map it
transposes, by `PresheafOfModules.range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule`.  There is no
hypothesis on `f` or on `F`: in particular `f` need not be a closed immersion, the ambient schemes
need not be affine, and `F` need not be locally quasi-coherent. -/
theorem range_moduleComparison_app_eq_fmapSubmodule
    (W : (A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)ᵒᵖ) :
    LinearMap.range ((moduleComparison M g).app W).hom = (fmapSubmodule M g).obj W :=
  PresheafOfModules.range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule _ (moduleFMap M g) W

/-- **The comparison morphism `c_f` factors through the sub-presheaf of `F_T` generated by the
image of the `f`-map.** -/
theorem moduleComparison_eq_comp_fmapSubmodule_ι :
    ((PresheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (restrictionFMap (crisRing S) g)).homEquiv
        (moduleRestriction M B) (fmapSubmodule M g).toPresheafOfModules).symm
      (PresheafOfModules.toGeneratedSubmodule _ (moduleFMap M g)) ≫ (fmapSubmodule M g).ι =
    moduleComparison M g :=
  PresheafOfModules.homEquivSymm_toGeneratedSubmodule_comp_ι _ (moduleFMap M g)

/-- **Under hypothesis (2) of [Stacks, Tag 07JN], `F_T` is locally generated by the image of the
`f`-map**, for every morphism of `Cris(X/S)` whose map on ambient schemes is a closed immersion:
every section of `F_T` is, on the members of an open covering of `T`, an `𝒪_T`-combination of
restrictions of sections in the image of `F_{T'} ⟶ f_* F_T`.

This is the source's passage from the surjectivity of `c_f` to the surjectivity of
`F_{T'} ⟶ f_* F_T`.  It is stated with local surjectivity on both sides, as hypothesis (2) is: the
restriction of a presheaf of modules to `T` is a presheaf and not a sheaf, so objectwise
surjectivity is the wrong condition. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_fmapSubmodule_ι (hM : IsSurjectiveComparison M)
    (hg : IsClosedImmersion g.hom.targetHom.hom) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology A.obj.thickening.target.scheme)
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringRestriction A)).map (fmapSubmodule M g).ι) := by
  have := hM g hg
  exact Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_fac _
    (((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringRestriction A)).map_comp _ _).symm.trans
      (congrArg _ (moduleComparison_eq_comp_fmapSubmodule_ι M g)))

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.CohomologyRestriction

end

end
